A||N||2||RiceBurner515||ECM testing?||||2||
Z||000000||RiceBurner515||11-09-2000||06:25 PM||||is there anyway you can check the car's ECM codes without those little machines? I've heard of using some jumper cables on something and looking at the dash for the number of blinks, does anybody know how to do this? I just want to check all of my sensors and stuff make sure they are good and whatnot.||||reg||2
Z||000001||Phil||11-09-2000||07:30 PM||||Run don't walk to your nearest Pep Boys, Autozone or whatever and get yourself a Haynes manual($14-16), it explains the whole procedure. If you own one of these little cars eventually you'll be doing repairs and most of the easy stuff is covered in the book||||reg||1
Z||000002||zeusrekning||11-09-2000||09:40 PM||||Assuming all are like my 87 coupe. <BR>Take the cig. lighter cover off and there is a little black "connector". if you look at it close the two bottom holes on the pass. side have brass rekonings in them. Join these two with wire, paper clip, Whatever and count the blinks on the Service engine soon light. Most auto parts stores have little things to put on your keychain to plug into the connector.||||reg||1
